# Chorus as published in 1929 (cut time, written here with quarter-note beats; "Am I" is the pickup)
Am I blue?
C4/ D4 A4/ ~A4(4) ~A4(2)
Am I blue?
C4/ D4 Bb4/ ~Bb4(4) ~Bb4(2)
Ain't these tears in these eyes tel-lin' you?
C4/ D4 C5/ ~C5(2) C#5/ D5 F4/ ~F4(2) Ab4/ G4 F4/ ~F4(2) ~F4 r r(2)
Am I blue?
C4/ D4 A4/ ~A4(4) ~A4(2)
You'd be too
C4/ D4 Bb4/ ~Bb4(4) ~Bb4(2)
if each plan with your man done fell through.
C4/ D4 C5/ ~C5(2) C#5/ D5 F4/ ~F4(2) Ab4/ G4 F4/ ~F4(4) ~F4(2)
Was a time I was his on-ly one,
C#4/ E4 C5/ ~C5(4) ~C5 E5 D5 C5 B4/ D5 B4/ ~B4(2) ~B4(2)
but now I'm the sad and lone-ly one.
D#4/ E4 B4/ ~B4(4) ~B4 D5 C5 B4 A4/ C5 C5/ ~C5(2)
"Lawd-y," was I gay
A4 G4/ r/ C4/ D4 A4/ ~A4(4) ~A4(2)
'til to-day.
C4/ D4 Bb4/ ~Bb4(4) ~Bb4(2)
Now he's gone and we're through,
